drm/sun4i: report the RGB connector as DSI

From ROCKNIX's 0155-sun4i-set-rgb-connector-as-DSI.patch, by Philippe Simons.

Upstream status: not upstream, and unlikely to be in this form -- it changes
the connector type unconditionally for every sun4i board, not just the ones
with an SPI-initialised DPI panel. Carried because ROCKNIX ships it and their
display works; if the panel attaches without it, drop it.

sun4i_rgb_init() registers the parallel RGB output as
DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_Unknown. This makes it DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DSI instead, so
the connector appears as DSI-1 rather than Unknown-1. Expect that name in
modetest output.

Unverified: whether this is cosmetic or load-bearing. Nothing in the panel
driver obviously requires a particular connector type, so treat the DSI naming
as the observable effect and not as proof of anything.
From f1f834beae9b9b76e9ef0ccc1c28ed0cc50ed9d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 24 Jul 2024 21:03:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] sun4i: set rgb connector as DSI

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_rgb.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_rgb.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_rgb.c
index dfb6acc42f02..e29c40086e5e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_rgb.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_rgb.c
@@ -222,7 +222,7 @@ int sun4i_rgb_init(struct drm_device *drm, struct sun4i_tcon *tcon)
 					 &sun4i_rgb_con_helper_funcs);
 		ret = drm_connector_init(drm, &rgb->connector,
 					 &sun4i_rgb_con_funcs,
-					 DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_Unknown);
+					 DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DSI);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(drm->dev, "Couldn't initialise the rgb connector\n");
 			goto err_cleanup_connector;
